      "nets": ["unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)"],
      "observed": "U2 pin 1 (VBAT) is on net unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1) and is not connected to VCC or any other net.",
      "expected": "VBAT should be connected to VCC (VDD) when no external battery is used, as recommended by the STM32L476 datasheet.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"65\") (name \"unconnected-(U2-VBAT-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U2\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\")))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere in the three .kicad_sch files or PCB.net/PCB.cir"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU's backup domain is left floating, which may cause increased current consumption, unreliable backup domain operation, or potential malfunction of the MCU.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain an anomaly: the STM32's VBAT pin (U2.1) is left unconnected instead of being tied to VCC, contrary to standard practice for a design without a backup battery."
}

